5,6]},{"text":"Lay the tortillas flat. Sprinkle a little cheese over one half of each, spread the bean mixture on top and cover with the rest of the cheese, dividing everything evenly. Fold the bare half over and press down gently.","uses":[8,7]},{"text":"Wipe out the skillet, set it over medium heat and brush it with a little of the remaining oil. Cook the quesadillas two at a time until the undersides are golden and crisp, {time 2-3 min}.","uses":[4]},{"text":"Flip them with a wide spatula and cook until the second side is golden and the cheese has melted, {time 2-3 min} more. Repeat with the rest, brushing the pan with a little more oil each time.","uses":[]},{"text":"Let the quesadillas rest on a cutting board for {time 1 min} so the cheese sets slightly, then cut each into wedges. Serve with the rest of the salsa and the sour cream.","uses":[2,9]}]}